    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "727-200\nIMPORTANT INFORMATION\nFOR OUR 727 FANJET PASSENGERS\nEMERGENCY EXITS\nThere are eight exits provided for your use. The chart below will\nshow you the one closest to your seat. The exits over the wings\nare removable windows. The two exits forward and the two side\nexits aft are doors which are equipped with fast operating\nevacuation slides.\nFWD CABIN DOORS\nFWD\nENTRY\nDOOR (LH Side)\nAND\nFWD\nGALLEY\nDOOR (RH Side)\nCLOSED\nROTATE\nHANDLE IN\nDIRECTION\nOF ARROW\nAND PUSH\nDOOR OUT\nOPEN\nSLIDE\nSTEP 1\nWINDOW EXITS\nSTEP 2\nPULL\nDOWN\nTHIS\nFLAP\nGRASP\nHANDLE\nAND\nPULL\nDOWN\nPULL\nTOP\nINWARD\nAND\nLIFT\nAFT SERVICE DOORS\nAFT\nSERVICE\nDOOR\n(LH and RH Side)\nPULL\nOUT\nHANDLE\nAND\nROTATE 180°\nPUSH\nDOOR\nOUT\nOPEN\nCLOSED\nSLIDE\nEMERGENCY EXITS\nENTRY\nDOOR\nAND 4\nESCAPE\nSLIDE\nGALLEY\nSERVICE\nDOOR\nAND\nESCAPE\nSLIDE\nWINDOW\nEXITS\nWINDOW\nLEXITS\nSERVICE\nDOOR\nBAND\nESCAPE\nSLIDE I\nSERVICE\nDOOR\nBAND\nESCAPE\nSLIDE\n*\n*REAR CABIN DOOR USED\nONLY AT DIRECTION OF\nFLIGHT CREW.\nPLACARDS GIVING\nSTEPS\nFOR OPERATION\nOF\nEVACUATION SLIDE\nARE LOCATED ON EACH\nDOOR. SLIDE IS SHOWN\nREADY FOR USE.\nPLEASE DO NOT REMOVE FROM AIRCRAFT\nSee Reverse Side\n2007.011.068",
      "PSA\n727\nIMPORTANT INFORMATION\nFOR OUR FANJET PASSENGERS\nEven though you may be an experienced air\ntraveler, there are certain features of this air-\ncraft with which you may not be familiar.\nAUTOMATIC OXYGEN SYSTEM\nThe higher altitudes at which this aircraft operates require the\nprompt use of the automatic oxygen system in case of any\nsudden change in cabin pressure. Should a decompression occur\noxygen masks will drop down. Pull nearest mask down to initiate\nflow of oxygen and promptly place over nose and mouth. Adjust\nheadband. Breathe normally.\nNO SMOKING\n60\nBREATHE\nNORMALLY\nFLOTATION EQUIPMENT\nFORWARD\nFACING\nSEAT\nBRACING POSITION\nREAR\nFACING\nSEAT\nIn the\nevent of a water landing,\ncushion\nmay be used\nas an aid\nto\nkeep afloat.\nGrasp the cushion at the\nrear, pull it forward and take it with\nyou.\nPlace arms through straps on\nbottom to retain cushion.\nSEAT BELT\nLIFT TO\nRELEASE\nEven if the \"SEAT BELT\" sign is turned off in flight, it is recommended\nthat you keep your seat belt loosely fastened, whenever you are in your\nseat.\nPLEASE DO NOT REMOVE FROM AIRCRAFT\nSEE REVERSE SIDE\n2-4-5/76"
    ],
